WEBVTT

00:01.500 --> 00:03.140
What choice do we have?

00:04.000 --> 00:06.550
The world is a cruel place!

00:15.590 --> 00:19.690
I swore... to kill them all!

00:20.020 --> 00:22.250
Every last one!

00:25.020 --> 00:26.430
And just like that...

00:26.430 --> 00:28.177
Everything changed.

00:31.022 --> 00:34.088
At that terrible moment, in our hearts, we knew.

00:37.088 --> 00:41.355
Home was a pen. Humanity... cattle.

00:58.230 --> 00:59.290
Eren!

01:00.900 --> 01:01.700
Eren...

01:06.580 --> 01:07.860
O, my friend!

01:07.860 --> 01:10.460
This is a victory for us!

01:10.520 --> 01:13.620
Our fame starts here!

01:13.660 --> 01:14.620
O, my friend!

01:14.620 --> 01:19.920
Let us celebrate this victory
for the next battle!

01:34.560 --> 01:40.100
"I died for naught" — I won't
let it end like that for you

01:40.100 --> 01:45.360
until I am the last one standing

01:45.360 --> 01:48.340
The enemy is cruel... We will kill...

01:48.340 --> 01:51.380
The enemy is colossal... We will jump...

01:51.380 --> 01:55.020
In our hands we hold blades of glory

01:55.020 --> 01:57.300
and sing in the name of victory

01:57.300 --> 02:01.940
We bear the wings of freedom on our backs

02:03.260 --> 02:09.380
Swearing iron determination upon our hearts,

02:09.400 --> 02:13.920
we slash apart the circle of idiocy

02:15.500 --> 02:17.820
and soar through the sky

02:17.880 --> 02:22.080
with our wings of freedom

02:36.010 --> 02:41.020
Wall: Assault on Stohess, Part 3

02:41.900 --> 02:43.700
brothers and sisters.

02:43.740 --> 02:49.390
Let us pray for the continued
strength of saints Maria, Rose, and Sina.

02:49.620 --> 02:51.650
May they stand firm.

02:52.410 --> 02:55.470
Their grace is a manifestation
of our good faith...

02:55.750 --> 02:58.920
We give thanks to the light
of the divine architect.

02:58.950 --> 03:00.920
He whose wisdom is the mortar;

03:00.950 --> 03:05.860
whose sublime love for his
creation is the steadfast stone.

03:05.890 --> 03:08.290
He, and he alone, protects us from

03:08.330 --> 03:12.100
the Titan scourge, in proportion
to our worship.

03:12.130 --> 03:15.700
Verily... innocence and
obedience are all he asks...

03:25.010 --> 03:28.140
No! Impossible!

03:39.660 --> 03:43.330
Dear God! Please! Not the wall!

03:44.030 --> 03:45.460
Stay away!

04:06.080 --> 04:09.690
Well I daresay it looks like our boy's
in control of himself this time.

04:09.720 --> 04:12.650
Yeah. Still, though...
There's no guarantee

04:12.650 --> 04:14.880
this will turn out any differently
than their last meeting.

04:16.440 --> 04:17.960
Come on, he
wouldn't have transformed...

04:18.000 --> 04:20.430
Unless he knew he could take her this time...

04:20.470 --> 04:21.900
He's got this, okay?

04:21.900 --> 04:22.650
I don't doubt that.

04:22.670 --> 04:24.890
But determination alone isn't
enough to win a fight.

04:24.940 --> 04:26.940
You of all people should know that.

04:28.640 --> 04:31.040
It'll take more
than that to beat Annie.

04:31.080 --> 04:32.540
A lot more.

04:34.610 --> 04:35.590
Damn it!

04:36.510 --> 04:38.350
She's making a
break for level ground!

04:38.380 --> 04:40.850
So much for our gear! What now?

04:41.410 --> 04:43.350
Split into two
teams and go around!

04:43.390 --> 04:44.570
Understood!

04:51.210 --> 04:52.460
C'mon, c'mon, c'mon!

04:52.960 --> 04:54.720
Son of a... where'd
they come from?

05:13.990 --> 05:17.650
Annie... always so cynical...

05:17.690 --> 05:21.030
Like every little thing around you
was pointless.

05:23.070 --> 05:25.320
Nothing
worth a second look.

05:28.200 --> 05:31.670
Every now and then, though, I
could see through the act...

05:31.700 --> 05:35.420
Especially when you were showing
off your fighting skills.

05:35.810 --> 05:38.480
Maybe hand-to-hand
combat didn't count for squat

05:38.510 --> 05:41.220
against our final
grade back at the academy...

05:41.410 --> 05:45.450
But to you? It was a
different story altogether.

05:45.520 --> 05:48.690
Yeah... about that much at least.

05:48.720 --> 05:51.790
It was
obvious you were a liar.

05:52.690 --> 05:54.560
Fighting's your whole world,

05:54.630 --> 05:57.460
but what exactly
are you fighting for?

05:57.530 --> 06:02.220
What could possibly have been worth
all this death and destruction?!

06:25.060 --> 06:26.590
Oh, God...

06:26.620 --> 06:28.360
Section commander, I hate to say it,

06:28.390 --> 06:30.790
but the city'll be debris
and corpses before long...

06:30.830 --> 06:32.560
Even if we manage to catch her.

06:32.600 --> 06:34.060
Well, then that's how it's gonna be!

06:34.100 --> 06:36.630
We're sticking to commander
Erwin's plan, got it?

06:37.000 --> 06:39.060
So stop babbling
and ready the nets.

06:39.090 --> 06:40.260
Right.

06:43.840 --> 06:45.340
Eren...

06:45.960 --> 06:47.790
We didn't
sign up for this.

06:47.950 --> 06:51.660
They... they didn't say there'd be
Titans fighting in the streets.

06:51.680 --> 06:53.650
No kidding. This is crazy.

06:54.850 --> 06:57.030
We've got two of 'em
hashing it out in the streets?

06:57.470 --> 06:58.120
Yes, Sir.

06:58.480 --> 07:00.990
The city's collapsing
like a house of cards.

07:01.330 --> 07:03.330
It's just... it's horrifying...

07:03.390 --> 07:05.860
We can only guess
how many casualties...

07:06.930 --> 07:10.670
Erwin! Your arrogance has
brought hell right to our door!

07:11.040 --> 07:12.240
I know.

07:15.610 --> 07:18.170
I acted entirely
on my own authority.

07:18.240 --> 07:20.550
And I offer no excuses.

07:24.420 --> 07:27.180
You knew what this would
do to us, you son of a bitch!

07:27.220 --> 07:29.350
You knew and
our lives be damned!

07:29.390 --> 07:31.780
Why? Damn you, why?

07:36.730 --> 07:38.180
For humanity.

07:39.030 --> 07:40.630
For victory.

07:40.670 --> 07:42.180
don't give me that!

07:42.900 --> 07:44.330
You're nothing but a traitor!

07:44.370 --> 07:46.650
I ought to kill you right here and now!

07:46.650 --> 07:48.720
None of the higher ups would fault me!

07:49.970 --> 07:52.140
Do as your
conscience dictates.

07:52.210 --> 07:54.180
My post is yours.

07:54.350 --> 07:56.570
The female Titan must not escape.

07:56.570 --> 08:00.730
Deployment is through peer and
Beirer is in command of provisions.

08:00.920 --> 08:02.150
Work with them closely.

08:02.190 --> 08:04.090
Do whatever is required
to ensure she doesn't...

08:04.160 --> 08:05.320
Shut up!

08:05.360 --> 08:09.270
Do... do you really believe...

08:09.290 --> 08:12.230
...this is for the good of us all?

08:12.260 --> 08:14.680
I have faith it's a step forward.

08:20.040 --> 08:22.140
Everyone, lower your rifles.

08:22.210 --> 08:24.040
Place this man under arrest.

08:24.080 --> 08:24.840
Sir!

08:25.780 --> 08:27.780
Deploy all troops immediately.

08:28.040 --> 08:31.350
As of now... focus on evacuation.

08:31.380 --> 08:32.990
Yes, Sir!

08:33.980 --> 08:35.100
Erwin...

08:35.130 --> 08:38.760
I hereby wash my hands of you and
leave you to the high court.

08:38.890 --> 08:41.750
I'll accept their judgment. Thank you, nile.

08:42.620 --> 08:44.740
Levi. For now, stay here.

08:44.800 --> 08:46.920
A pointless death wouldn't suit you.

08:47.060 --> 08:48.860
No, I doubt it would...

08:49.470 --> 08:51.570
Any more than it suits anyone else.

08:57.840 --> 09:03.100
To rise above monsters, we
have to abandon our humanity.

09:04.010 --> 09:06.770
What we fight, we become...

09:10.090 --> 09:11.820
...fire with fire.

09:16.260 --> 09:18.830
Look at her.
Annie can do it.

09:24.840 --> 09:26.010
Annie...

09:27.300 --> 09:28.730
Annie!

09:49.330 --> 09:50.540
Annie...

09:53.060 --> 09:54.800
I believe in you.

09:54.830 --> 09:57.170
I'm always on your side.

10:12.750 --> 10:18.810
I... will... kill them...

10:19.960 --> 10:22.600
Every last one!

10:47.250 --> 10:48.730
Eren!

10:51.490 --> 10:53.220
What is he...?

10:53.720 --> 10:54.880
Help him!

10:54.910 --> 10:57.060
No! With the state he's in,

10:57.060 --> 10:59.160
it's probably best that
we keep our distance.

11:16.310 --> 11:17.810
God.

11:45.280 --> 11:46.910
She's headed up the wall!

11:46.910 --> 11:48.430
She's trying to escape!

12:00.560 --> 12:04.360
No, no, no! We can't let her get away!

12:06.230 --> 12:07.800
I won't let her!

12:22.980 --> 12:24.380
It's over, Annie.

12:25.920 --> 12:27.250
Now fall.

12:35.690 --> 12:36.790
Annie...

12:38.520 --> 12:40.160
I'm so sorry.

12:41.370 --> 12:44.070
I don't
expect you to forgive me.

12:45.860 --> 12:48.510
But... please...

12:49.300 --> 12:50.820
Please just...

12:54.080 --> 12:57.920
Stand your ground. Stand your ground

12:57.920 --> 13:00.620
even if the whole world stands against you.

13:02.350 --> 13:08.390
Die... all of you... everything...

13:08.430 --> 13:10.430
They'll despise you...

13:10.800 --> 13:12.650
They won't understand.

13:13.080 --> 13:16.860
But I will. Your dad always will.

13:17.970 --> 13:21.410
Oh, no! He's gonna devour her whole!

13:21.410 --> 13:22.660
Eren! Back off!

13:22.660 --> 13:23.530
don't do it!

13:23.530 --> 13:27.410
This... is freedom!

13:28.120 --> 13:30.310
Promise me you'll return...

13:31.540 --> 13:33.120
That's all I ask.

13:51.400 --> 13:53.710
Wha... what's he doing?

13:56.370 --> 13:57.680
Son of a...?

13:59.440 --> 14:01.110
They're merging?

14:10.450 --> 14:11.800
Stop it, Eren!

14:18.960 --> 14:21.660
It's not a good idea
to eat our key evidence...

14:21.700 --> 14:23.400
You idiot.

15:11.620 --> 15:12.780
Eren.

15:13.720 --> 15:16.890
Mikasa... is Annie...?

15:29.120 --> 15:30.230
Damn it!

15:30.730 --> 15:33.880
All the shit we've been through
and this is what we get?

15:34.480 --> 15:36.780
Annie! Wake up!

15:36.830 --> 15:39.460
C'mon, face the
music! You owe us!

15:39.520 --> 15:43.220
don't be a coward!
I know you can hear me!

15:45.330 --> 15:46.530
That's enough.

15:48.320 --> 15:49.340
It's over.

15:54.310 --> 15:56.480
Someone get me a wire net!

15:56.480 --> 15:58.880
This thing belongs
deep underground!

15:58.880 --> 16:00.140
Understood!

16:01.670 --> 16:03.430
What have we done?

16:03.470 --> 16:08.200
If we can't get any answers out of her,
then what was the point of all this?

16:08.590 --> 16:11.530
We're left with nothing
but countless casualties,

16:11.530 --> 16:14.770
ruined lives,
and unanswered questions.

16:14.770 --> 16:16.540
All for what?

16:27.130 --> 16:28.990
Well, it was a valiant effort.

16:29.030 --> 16:30.980
Can't win 'em all though, right?

16:30.980 --> 16:31.730
Right.

16:31.760 --> 16:35.360
At the very least the scout
regiment's been exonerated.

16:35.360 --> 16:38.100
Sure, by the skin of its teeth, but still.

16:40.050 --> 16:42.180
Let's hope the brass agrees.

16:51.750 --> 16:55.420
As you might imagine,
we have many questions.

16:56.660 --> 16:59.490
If the target's identity
was beyond all doubt,

16:59.560 --> 17:03.110
why would you neglect to request
aid from the military police?

17:03.110 --> 17:05.990
Discretion. We had
reason to believe she was

17:05.990 --> 17:08.250
operating in conjunction
with other insiders.

17:08.250 --> 17:12.570
I felt it was necessary to involve
only those well above suspicion, Sir.

17:12.800 --> 17:16.810
Yes. And the price of your "discretion"
was the near obliteration of Stohess.

17:16.840 --> 17:17.900
Well done.

17:17.900 --> 17:20.540
I didn't foresee
the damage's scale, Sir.

17:20.850 --> 17:22.280
Blame my incompetence.

17:22.310 --> 17:24.320
Blame isn't going to rebuild my roof!

17:24.380 --> 17:26.320
If the female Titan
were left to roam free...

17:26.360 --> 17:28.310
The wall was subject to breach...

17:28.330 --> 17:31.190
And the damage to Stohess
would've been beyond devastating.

17:31.220 --> 17:32.520
Perhaps.

17:32.690 --> 17:33.720
Erwin...

17:33.760 --> 17:36.660
You have me grasping at
straws to exonerate you...

17:36.700 --> 17:40.830
What I need is proof that your tactics
yielded some manner of benefit.

17:40.870 --> 17:44.300
Granted, Annie Leonhart is
rendered innocuous,

17:44.340 --> 17:46.640
but also essentially useless.

17:46.670 --> 17:49.170
Yes, Sir. That she is.

17:49.640 --> 17:50.700
Are you saying...

17:51.440 --> 17:53.130
It was all for nothing...?

17:59.320 --> 18:00.090
Hey.

18:09.330 --> 18:10.890
You feel okay?

18:12.910 --> 18:13.630
Yeah...

18:15.300 --> 18:18.210
In fact it's weird how "okay" I feel.

18:20.090 --> 18:23.400
So, is... Annie still stuck in that thing?

18:23.890 --> 18:25.160
Uh-huh.

18:25.610 --> 18:28.440
Yeah... you'd think after all we sacrificed

18:28.440 --> 18:30.480
to get her back, fate
would cut us a little slack.

18:30.550 --> 18:34.320
It's humbling, knowing how far
she'll go to keep her secrets.

18:34.390 --> 18:37.740
Humbling? More like infuriating.

18:38.170 --> 18:40.300
Why'd you let her go, Eren?

18:44.270 --> 18:46.450
You did... didn't you?

18:47.550 --> 18:49.160
You gave her an out.

18:50.400 --> 18:54.670
I know. I didn't mean to, I...

18:54.710 --> 18:56.810
I just couldn't help it.

18:58.340 --> 19:02.090
When I saw her face, I just froze...

19:05.040 --> 19:08.480
Armin Arlelt, and Jean Kirschtein...

19:08.520 --> 19:09.850
You two are up first.

19:09.920 --> 19:10.920
Yes, Sir.

19:10.960 --> 19:12.560
Debriefing time.

19:12.590 --> 19:14.120
See you later, I guess.

19:14.160 --> 19:15.430
Sure.

19:27.640 --> 19:31.450
Honestly... it felt kinda... good.

19:32.740 --> 19:34.380
Just letting go...

19:34.410 --> 19:37.160
My body, my mind, everything...

19:38.420 --> 19:40.120
For a minute it was almost...

19:40.190 --> 19:41.950
Like I wanted to die...

19:42.020 --> 19:43.630
Eren, stop it!

19:46.690 --> 19:48.930
don't worry,
I'm better now.

19:59.700 --> 20:00.740
I'm glad...

20:02.170 --> 20:04.080
I'm glad you're back...

20:09.650 --> 20:11.950
I can't get my head wrapped around it.

20:11.980 --> 20:16.090
This whole fighting fire with
fire business or whatever.

20:16.120 --> 20:18.660
Is that really the
only option we've got?

20:18.890 --> 20:22.590
Not necessarily. Just the only
one that's presented itself.

20:23.800 --> 20:25.660
And now we know Eren can do it.

20:27.970 --> 20:32.890
Yeah, well... if it's that easy for the
fight to turn us all into monsters...

20:33.710 --> 20:36.060
...then maybe we don't deserve to win.

20:46.990 --> 20:48.230
Go on.

21:06.140 --> 21:10.010
No one ever promised us
we'd come out of this unscathed.

21:10.870 --> 21:14.610
For nothing? I believe this latest tragedy

21:14.610 --> 21:17.340
has moved us forward
by leaps and bounds, Sir.

21:20.750 --> 21:22.650
Not long ago, we hadn't even imagined

21:22.690 --> 21:25.790
the possibility of humans
transforming into Titans.

21:25.820 --> 21:28.560
Now, we're not only aware of
the enemy in our midst...

21:28.690 --> 21:30.590
We've managed to capture one of them.

21:30.660 --> 21:35.940
Make no mistake, there are more out there.
And we will hunt down every last one.

21:36.570 --> 21:38.330
The initiative is ours.

21:38.700 --> 21:40.170
Starting now...

21:41.488 --> 21:44.032
We launch an attack on
the Titans within our walls!

21:48.750 --> 21:53.680
The scout regiment's recall to the capital
and Eren's incarceration were rescinded.

21:53.720 --> 21:57.720
Instead, they were charged with guarding
Annie Leonhart in her holding cell

21:57.760 --> 22:01.790
deep underground, where they
kept strict vigil day and night.

22:02.430 --> 22:03.960
Sadly, however...

22:04.030 --> 22:06.430
It would
take a far longer time...

22:06.460 --> 22:08.800
And cost a
great many more lives...

22:08.840 --> 22:13.820
for humanity to discover the true nature...
of what it held captive.
